# SlintScanners — Installation

slintscanners is a build-dependency, not a global tool.
It runs automatically during `cargo build` via `build.rs`.

---

## Add to a Slint project

### Cargo.toml

```toml
[build-dependencies]
slintscanners = { git = "https://github.com/lpmwfx/SlintScanners" }
```

### build.rs

```rust
fn main() {
    slintscanners::scan_project();
}
```

That is all. The scanner runs on every `cargo build` and emits
`cargo:warning=...` for each violation.

---

## Configuration (optional)

Create `proj/rulestools.toml` in the project root to control which
checks run and whether violations block the build:

```toml
[slintscanners]
enabled       = true   # false = scanner disabled entirely
deny          = false  # true = panic and block build on any error

check_tokens       = true  # hardcoded colors, px, %, ms, numbers
check_strings      = true  # string literals in state fields
check_structure    = true  # one component per file
check_events       = true  # invalid callback usage
check_mother_child = true  # stateless child enforcement
check_string_states = true # string literal state comparisons
check_architecture = true  # single-gateway callback rule

exclude = [
    "**/generated/**",   # skip generated .slint files
]
```

All checks are on by default. Set `deny = true` to make violations
block the build (useful in CI).

---

## What is scanned

`.slint` files under `ui/` (or `src/` if no `ui/` directory exists).
Workspace roots are detected automatically.

### Three-tier hierarchy enforced

```
Mother  (app-window.slint, inherits Window)
├── imports Views    — stateless screens, only Mother imports these
└── imports Widgets  — generic, reusable, importable by anyone

Views   (ui/views/)
├── in property + callback only — no in-out property
└── may NOT import sibling views

Widgets (ui/widgets/ or ui/components/)
├── in property + callback only — no in-out property
└── zero literals — tokens only (no hardcoded colors, px, ms, ...)
```

When a violation is found the error message tells you which tier the
component belongs to and whether to extract it to `widgets/` or keep
it as a view-specific child.

---

## Update

To pull the latest version:

```bash
cargo update slintscanners
```

No version pinning — always tracks the latest commit on `main`.
